Every device in a network needs
	Ip address
	subnet mask
	default gateway
	dns server
Manually configuring this for every device isnt scalable so we use Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP).
DHCP automates IP configuration using a client-server model.
DHCP application layer protocol
It runs overs UDP
	Client port: 68
	Server port: 67
It follows a 4 step process called as DORA

STEP 1: DHCPDISCOVER

A device doesnt have ip address when it boots 
It sends a broadcast packet

Source IP: 0.0.0.0
Destination IP: 255.255.255.255
UDP 68 -> 67

STEP 2: DHCPOFFER

The DHCP server receives this request and does the following:
Available IP pool
Mac address of the client
Lease database

The server replies with
The ip address
subnet mask 
default gateway
DNS
Lease time

This could be a broadcast or a unicat.JUst on offer the ip isnt permanently assigned yet.

STEP 3: DHCPREQUEST

The client receives multiple offers.
It chooses one server and broadcasts that it has accepted this particular offered ip. 
This broadcast informs the other DHCP servers to withdraw their offers.

STEP 4: DHCPACK

The server confirms that the ip has been assigned and it starts the lease timer.

LEASE MECHANISM

IP assignment is not permanent.

When lease reaches 50% time:
	Client sends DHCPREQUEST directly to server to renew.
	If server responds with DHCPACK:
	Lease extended.

If not:
	Client eventually drops IP and restarts DORA.



